  "label": "Historical Context of Antisemitism in Architectural Spaces",
  "description": "The use of grand architectural spaces (like churches or mosques) in antisemitic imagery to imply Jewish people are intruders or unwelcome in places of worship or historical significance. This reflects historical antisemitic narratives that sought to exclude Jews from sacred or public spaces.",
